  "worked_solution": "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-4$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=-4.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=1,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}\u20615x+Q\\operatorname{sin}\u20615x)+{e}^{x}(-5P\\operatorname{sin}\u20615x+5Q\\operatorname{cos}\u20615x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=1$ into the above to get\n\n$$\nP+5Q=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=-4$ gives $Q=1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}\u20615x+\\operatorname{sin}\u20615x).\n$$",
